    {
      "filename": "Edgbaston - Aug 2005 - Eng v Aus - Andrew Flintoff - Six! (3764801159).jpg",
      "title": "File:Edgbaston - Aug 2005 - Eng v Aus - Andrew Flintoff - Six! (3764801159).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/Edgbaston_-_Aug_2005_-_Eng_v_Aus_-_Andrew_Flintoff_-_Six%21_%283764801159%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edgbaston_-_Aug_2005_-_Eng_v_Aus_-_Andrew_Flintoff_-_Six!_(3764801159).jpg",
      "width": 992,
      "height": 766,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Gareth Williams from Redhill, England",
      "description": "I was lucky enough to get a ticket for Day 2 of this momentous test. I do a quiznight at my then local town of Newbury organized by a man whose brother is scorer for Warwickshire. As we were having lunch on day 2 the brother joined us and asked my friend if he knew anyone who would like a ticket for day 3. I kept quiet and looked at the floor before my friend asked if I would like it. I accepted. This ticket was for a guest of the ECB so lunch next day I joined the English players WAGS and families and sat with the whole travelling Australian entourage in the Ryder Stand. It is fair to say I thoroughly enjoyed myself as well as witnessing two of the greatest deliveries in Ashes history; both the last ball of the day. I also witnessed Flintoff hit this ball for 6. Not a bad picture using a Canon G3 stills camera I thought.",
      "dateCreated": "2009-07-28 12:53",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "edgbaston-cricket-ground-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcqd",
      "smallPath": "_m/g/c/q/d/edgbaston-cricket-ground-wp/edgbaston-aug-2005-eng-v-aus-a-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Edgbaston - May 2006 - Pearl's a Singer and a bit of a Show-off (4861838496).jpg",
      "title": "File:Edgbaston - May 2006 - Pearl's a Singer and a bit of a Show-off (4861838496).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/Edgbaston_-_May_2006_-_Pearl%27s_a_Singer_and_a_bit_of_a_Show-off_%284861838496%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edgbaston_-_May_2006_-_Pearl%27s_a_Singer_and_a_bit_of_a_Show-off_(4861838496).jpg",
      "width": 1255,
      "height": 994,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Gareth Williams from Redhill, England",
      "description": "Wandering round the ground at the tea-break during England's game against Sri Lanka I came across this jazz band performing for the amusement of those unlucky enough to be queueing for either tea or the toilets or both. I don't remember if they were any good but I do remember that the woman very much enjoyed her part in the proceedings and being the centre of attention. It was all very civilized but the tea was only tepid by the time I found somewhere to perch uncomfortably.\n\nAnyway I thought she was well worth a snap. So were the drummer's sideburns.",
      "dateCreated": "2006-05-26 13:20",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "edgbaston-cricket-ground-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcqd",
      "smallPath": "_m/g/c/q/d/edgbaston-cricket-ground-wp/edgbaston-may-2006-pearl-s-a-s-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Edgbaston 2005 - Eng v Aus - Day 3 - Girl in the Crowd - For Boxing Day 2010 (5300453137).jpg",
      "title": "File:Edgbaston 2005 - Eng v Aus - Day 3 - Girl in the Crowd - For Boxing Day 2010 (5300453137).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/12/Edgbaston_2005_-_Eng_v_Aus_-_Day_3_-_Girl_in_the_Crowd_-_For_Boxing_Day_2010_%285300453137%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edgbaston_2005_-_Eng_v_Aus_-_Day_3_-_Girl_in_the_Crowd_-_For_Boxing_Day_2010_(5300453137).jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 1200,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Gareth Williams from Redhill, England",
      "description": "This is part of the excited Edgbaston crowd during England's march to victory on Day 3 of that amazing Test Match. At the end of this day England appeared to be cruising to victory before Shane Warne and Brett Lee took the Aussies so close to snatching the game from us.\nI have put this picture up tonight as a celebration of England's wonderful performance in bowling Australia out for 98 on Boxing Day at the Melbourne Test. With luck and a following wind we will have retained the Ashes by 2 o'clock tonight and we will all be in party mood.\n\nCome on England.",
      "dateCreated": "2005-08-06 14:01",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "edgbaston-cricket-ground-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcqd",
      "smallPath": "_m/g/c/q/d/edgbaston-cricket-ground-wp/edgbaston-2005-eng-v-aus-day-3-small.webp"
    }
